   "id": 243582,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "An extremely efficient solar panel is designed with an energy gap of 1.4 eV. If shining a light on the panel causes a current to flow and the temperature of the panel to increase slightly, what can you say about the wavelength of the light?\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 763717,
     "content_html": "The light’s wavelength was about 837 nm."
    },
    {
     "id": 763716,
     "content_html": "The light’s wavelength was about 886 nm."
    },
    {
     "id": 763715,
     "content_html": "The light’s wavelength was about 908 nm."
    },
    {
     "id": 763714,
     "content_html": "The light’s wavelength was about 950 nm."
    }
